MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The flash drive feels useful because I move between computers and already use removable storage; it offers a direct USB connection without a microSD adapter.",
    "The powered USB hub fits my growing desk setup because I use several USB accessories, and individual switches would make them easier to manage."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The smart speaker, streaming stick, tablet and portable speaker introduce activities I have not shown a current need for; my recent purchases center on connecting, organizing and maintaining computer equipment.",
    "The earbuds and longer HDMI cable resemble things I already own, but similarity alone does not give me a reason to replace or duplicate them. The optical cable also needs a specific connection project I do not currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning electronics seems to have been taken as interest in more electronics generally, even when the suggested devices serve different purposes from my current setup.",
    "My headphone and cable purchases seem to have been treated as ongoing demand for more headphones and cables, without considering whether those needs are already covered."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet accessories, headphone mount, backpack and electric duster suggest I am making my existing equipment more connected, organized, portable and easier to maintain.",
    "I need a clear additional use before buying another accessory: the flash drive and hub offer one, while the Bluetooth adapter depends on whether a particular computer lacks Bluetooth."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in practical computer accessories but stretch it into demand for unrelated devices and duplicates of equipment I already have."
}
